    <string name="meaning_current" formatted="false">Positive values are current going into the battery, negative values are current coming out of it. Speed and time estimates use the average of the last readings. Charging slows down near 100%, so the real time to full is usually longer.</string>
    <string name="meaning_voltage_low">Low voltage. The battery is nearly empty or the phone is under heavy load.</string>
    <string name="meaning_voltage_normal">A healthy reading. Voltage rises while charging and drops as you use the phone.</string>
    <string name="meaning_voltage_high">High voltage, common near the end of a charge.</string>
    <string name="meaning_voltage_too_high">Above the usual range. If it stays like this, unplug the charger and check it.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_too_cold">Very cold. Batteries lose capacity and charge poorly in the cold. Avoid charging until the phone warms up.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_cold">Cool. The battery may hold a bit less charge while cold.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_normal">Ideal temperature for the battery.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_warm">Normal while charging, gaming or using the camera. Staying warm for hours wears the battery a little faster.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_hot">Hot. Give the phone a break, take it out of the case or stop charging for a while.</string>
    <string name="meaning_temp_too_hot">Too hot. Stop charging and heavy use until it cools down.</string>
    <string name="meaning_level_critical">Almost empty. Charge soon so the phone does not shut down.</string>
    <string name="meaning_level_low">Low. A good time to charge.</string>
    <string name="meaning_level_good" formatted="false">Batteries last longer when kept between 20% and 80%.</string>
    <string name="meaning_level_high" formatted="false">Above 80%. Fine now and then, but staying full for long periods wears the battery a bit faster.</string>
    <string name="meaning_power_slow">Slow charging. The charger, the cable or what the phone is doing may be limiting the speed.</string>
    <string name="meaning_power_normal">Normal charging speed.</string>
    <string name="meaning_power_fast">Fast charging: the charger and the cable are working well together.</string>
    <string name="meaning_use_light">Light use. The battery is lasting well.</string>
    <string name="meaning_use_normal">Normal use.</string>
    <string name="meaning_use_heavy">Heavy use. Screen brightness, games, camera or navigation drain the battery faster.</string>
    <string name="meaning_status_charging">Charging normally.</string>
    <string name="meaning_status_discharging">Running on the battery.</string>
    <string name="meaning_status_full">The battery is full.</string>
    <string name="meaning_source_ac">A wall charger, usually the fastest way to charge.</string>
    <string name="meaning_source_usb">A USB port, such as a computer or a power bank. Usually slower than a wall charger.</string>
    <string name="meaning_source_wireless">A wireless charger. Convenient, but slower and warmer than a cable.</string>
    <string name="meaning_source_battery">No charger connected.</string>
    <string name="meaning_health_good">The battery still holds most of its original charge.</string>
    <string name="meaning_health_fair">Some normal wear. The battery holds a bit less than when it was new.</string>
    <string name="meaning_health_worn">Noticeable wear. The battery holds clearly less than when it was new and empties faster.</string>
    <string name="meaning_health_poor">Heavy wear. Consider replacing the battery if it runs out too quickly.</string>
    <string name="meaning_health_unknown">Set the design capacity in Settings to estimate the battery health.</string>
    <string name="meaning_technology" formatted="false">Lithium batteries last longer when kept cool and charged between 20% and 80%. A full charge now and then is fine.</string>
    <string name="meaning_cycles" formatted="false">One cycle is using 100% of the battery charge, even if spread over several days. Many phone batteries keep around 80% of their capacity after 500 to 800 cycles.</string>
    <string name="note_voltage">This is the battery voltage. Fast chargers use a higher voltage on the cable, and the phone lowers it for the battery. The voltage jumps a little when you plug or unplug the charger.</string>
    <string name="note_temperature">Android reports the battery temperature, which follows how warm the whole phone is.</string>
    <string name="note_power">Power is voltage times current: how fast energy goes into or out of the battery. While charging it is lower than the charger power: part runs the phone, part is lost as heat, and it drops as the battery fills.</string>
    <string name="note_health">Health is the estimated full charge today compared with the design capacity. The phone battery check only flags failures such as overheating.</string>
